    "Incoming\nYour Way to Augsburg\nWelcome to the School of Business at Technical University of Applied Sciences Augsburg! Have you already been nominated by your home university? And are you coming to us as an exchange student for one or two semesters?\nAre you Exchange Student or Degree-Seeking Student?\nEvery year, we are delighted to welcome around 100 students from all over the world to our School of Business.\nSince we know how new this experience can be, we’d like to help you find the information that’s right for you.\nExchange students are visiting students who study with us for one or two semester.\nDegree-seeking students are those who plan to complete their entire degree program at THA.\nIncoming Exchange\nDegree-Seeking Students\nEverything at a Glance for Exchange Students\nHere you'll find the most important information regarding academic matters during your study abroad program at the School of Business.\nBusiness Courses in English for Bachelor's and Master's Students\nAcademic Calendar\nImportant Downloads for Exchange Students\nTestimonials\nFrequently Asked Questions\nContact Person\nApplication\nBusiness Courses in English for Bachelor's and Master's Students\nThe School of Business offers numerous business courses in English, primarily from the “International Management (B.A.)” and “International Business & Finance (M.A.)” degree programs, which are open to our exchange students.\nIn addition, many elective courses are offered university-wide, covering a broad spectrum of subject areas.\nBusiness Courses in English\nAcademic Calendar\nSummer Semester 2026\nThe following is a list of the most important dates for the 2026 summer semester.\nDate\nPeriod\nSemester Duration\nMarch 15, 2026 – September 30, 2026\nEaster Break\nApril 2–7, 2026\n“Incoming Students Meet Outgoing Students” Event\nApril 22, 2026\nPentecost Break\nMay 26, 2026\nDay after Corpus Christi\nJune 5, 2026\nExam Registration for the Summer Semester 2026\nApril 17 – June 8, 2026\nRe-registration for the 2026–27 winter semester\nJune 1–19, 2026\nCourse Assessments for AW Courses\nJune 22, 2026, and June 20, 2026\nExam period for the School of Business\nJune 29 – July 17, 2026\nAnnouncement of exam results for the 2026 summer semester\nJuly 30, 2026\nSemester break\nAugust 1 – September 30, 2026\nWinter Semester 2026/27\nThe following is a list of the most important dates for the 2026/27 winter semester.\nDate\nPeriod\nSemester Duration\nOctober 1, 2026 – March 14, 2027\nExam Registration for the Winter Semester 2026/27\nNovember 2, 2026 – December 3, 2026\nRe-enrollment for the Summer Semester 2027\nNovember 30, 2026 – January 8, 2027\nChristmas break\nDecember 24, 2026 – January 6, 2027\nAssessments for AW Courses\nJanuary 16, 2027, and January 18, 2027\nExam Period for the School of Business\nTBD\nAnnouncement of exam results for the 2025–26 winter semester\nFebruary 11, 2027\nSemester break\nFebruary 14, 2027 – March 15, 2027\nImportant Downloads for Exchange Students\nExample-Transcript_of_Records.pdf\n817 KB\nStudy-Program-BA-International_Management.pdf\n40 KB\nStudy-Program-BA-Business-Administration-German_B2.pdf\n56 KB\nTestimonials from Former Exchange Students\nTran Duc Minh\nYuan Ze University, Taiwan\nThe most interesting thing about Germany is its diversity—especially the differences between the north and the south. There are friendly people everywhere.\nEvery teacher I met at THA was helpful and answered my questions whenever I was struggling with my classes.\nAngela Pertrosillo\nUniversity of Modena, Italy\nI fell in love with the buildings, the colors, the large green spaces, and most of all the traditional Bavarian clothing—the dirndl and lederhosen. I loved Oktoberfest, even though I'm not the biggest fan of beer. It was the best experience of my life.\nChiara Carpi\nUniversity of Modena, Italy\n\"Five months during which I met people from all over the world and discovered new cultures and countries. I had to step out of my comfort zone and become very independent. I really enjoyed living on my own for the first time and just relying on myself.\"\nFrequently Asked Questions\nWhat courses can I take?\nYou can take\nbusiness courses in English\nat the bachelor's or master's level. You can also choose from a wide range of electives offered university-wide.\nCan I take business courses in German language?\nIf you can demonstrate that you have at least a B2 level, you can also choose courses taught in German.\nHow do I register for my classes?\nCourse registration takes place via our online learning platform,\nMoodle\n. That is also where most of your communication with your instructors will take place, and where course materials will be made available.\nWhere can I find the class schedules?\nYou can view the class schedules online on\nWebuntis\n.\nHow do I register for the exams?\nExam registration takes place with Ms. Wetzel. The date for this will be communicated to exchange students well in advance.\nIt is important to register for the correct exams within the specified time frame; otherwise, you will not be able to take the exams.\nWhat grading system is used at THA?\nGrades are assigned as follows:\n1.0/1.3 = A (Excellent) — Outstanding performance with only minor errors\n1.7/2.0 = B (Very Good) – Above average, but with some errors\n2.3/2.7 = C (Good) – Generally solid work with a number of notable errors.\n3.0/3.3 = D (Satisfactory) – Fair, but with significant shortcomings\n3.7/4.0 = E (Sufficient) – Performance meets the minimum requirements\n5.0 = F (Fail)\nWhen is the exam period?\nThe exact dates of the exams at the School of Business can be found in the\nAcademic Calendar\n.\nHow do I know where my exams will be held?\nThe exam rooms and times will be posted well in advance in the Moodle course\n“1. Program Information”\nunder “School of Business.”\nWhen will I find out my exam results?\nThe exact date when exam results will be announced can be found in\nthe\nAcademic Calendar\n. Grades can then be viewed in the\n“HIS Exam Management”\nportal.\nWhen will I receive my transcript of records?\nThe transcript of records can be printed via the\n“HIS Exam Administration”\nportal\nafter grades are released.\nWhat do I need to do before I go home?\nIt is important that you meet with the International Coordinators at the School of Business and the International Office to complete any additional formalities, if necessary.\nKey Contacts at the School of Business\nHelene Wetzel\nStaff\nSchool of Business\n+49 821 5586 2936\nhelene.wetzel(at)tha.de\nApplication\nHave we sparked your interest in studying abroad at our School of Business?\nIf so, please feel free to visit our International Office’s website to learn more about the current application process and fees.\nWe look forward to welcoming you to our school soon. See you soon!\nInformation on Applying for Exchange Students"
  ],
